{
  "requirement": "After one valid judgment, the harness MUST write the subject text, submitted\ndetermination and rationale, and recorded inputs using the existing evidence\nschema. {cite}`requirements.ci.schema`\nBy default, it MUST write the subject's evidence file. With `--stdout`, it MUST\nemit a single evidence JSON object followed by a newline to stdout and MUST NOT\ncreate or change evidence files or directories. All three outcomes MUST be\nwritten to the selected destination as completed assessments; their validation\nstatus MUST follow {cite}`requirements.ci.determination`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "## Judgment\n\nThe implementation meets `requirements.authoring.persistence`, and the tests cover its main points. Two small marking quirks are noted at the end. I don't count them as gaps.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- **Record contents.** `assess` (`src/authoring/mod.rs`, fn `assess`) builds the record only after exactly one valid `submit_judgment`. The object is `{ <requirement|example>: sources.subject_text, determination: judgment.to_value(), rationale, inputs: sources.recorded_inputs() }`, which matches the existing evidence schema. Failures, missing submissions, multiple submissions, and denied reads all return before this point, so nothing is written for them.\n- **Outcome mapping.** `Judgment::to_value` (`src/judgment.rs`) serializes `true`, `false` and `{FIXME:[…]}`. All three go through the same write path and are recorded as `completed` assessments. Nothing special-cases `false`.\n- **Default destination (single subject).** `configured_assessment` writes `evidence/<name>.json`, creating the directory first, as pretty JSON plus a trailing newline.\n- **Default destination (batch).** `write_record` in `src/authoring/batch.rs` writes the same pending record, using a temp file and atomic persist. `PendingAssessment::persisted` then marks `evidence_written` and the usage outcome `completed`.\n- **`--stdout`.** In `configured_assessment`, `EvidenceOutput::Stdout` writes only the pretty JSON plus `\\n` to stdout and flushes. It never touches the project's `evidence/` path. Usage state is created outside the project, and `usage_state_root` refuses a state root inside the project.\n- **Determination status.** The record carries the determination verbatim. Validation status is left to `requirements.ci.determination`, which tests in `src/evidence.rs` cover separately.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **`stdout_emits_only_evidence_json_without_changing_project_files`** (`tests/authoring_cli.rs`):\n  - It covers true, false and FIXME, with and without verbose.\n  - It parses stdout with `serde_json::from_slice` (so there is exactly one object) and checks it ends in a newline.\n  - It checks the requirement text, determination, rationale and inputs.\n  - It checks that existing evidence is byte-identical, and that the evidence directory is not created when it was absent.\n- **`false_is_a_completed_assessment`, `verbose_single_author_reports_only_false_rationale_without_source_inputs`:** The default file mode is exercised for false and true. The tests check determination, rationale, inputs, no source text in the inputs, and usage `completed`.\n- **Batch tests** (`tests/authoring_batch.rs`): `terminal_progress_distinguishes_judgments_from_authoring_errors` has false and FIXME records written alongside true ones. The denied-read tests check that no evidence is written for an aborted assessment and that the other assessments' evidence is kept.\n- **`explicit_untracked_reads_abort_without_another_request_or_evidence_write`:** A failed assessment emits nothing on stdout and leaves existing evidence unchanged.\n- **`failed_evidence_write_keeps_the_accepted_judgment_in_usage`:** A write failure is reported, with `evidence_written` false.\n- **`live_bedrock_authoring`:** It checks the stdout path against a real provider.\n\n## Minor observations (not gaps)\n\n- `PendingAssessment` is marked `{cite}` only. It is a data holder, and the behavior it supports (`persisted`, `write_record`) is marked `{impl}`.\n- The `--stdout` flag to `EvidenceOutput::Stdout` mapping in `main.rs` sits under the invocation markers. The emission itself is marked `{impl}` for persistence.\n- The atomic temp-file replace in `write_record` is a batch-safety detail. It is consistent with \"write the subject's evidence file\" and adds no behavior that conflicts with the requirement.",
  "inputs": [
